---
// Disclaimer and privacy: linked from the footer of every page, beside Cookies.
// It holds what used to be spread over the About page: the disclaimer, what Good
// Call is not, and what happens to your answers and data.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer and privacy"
  description="Good Call is for education only. What it is not, and how your answers and data are kept: on your device, not shared, unless you are registered through an institution."
  path="/disclaimer/"
>
  <h1>Disclaimer and privacy</h1>

  <div class="longform">
    <section class="page-section prose" id="disclaimer" aria-labelledby="disclaimer-title">
      <h2 id="disclaimer-title">Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Good Call is provided for general education only. The scenarios, answers and reasons are teaching material.
        They are not legal, medical, psychological, safeguarding or employment advice, and they are no substitute for
        advice from a qualified professional about your own situation.
      </p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>
          Not legal advice. Where a law is mentioned, it is the law in England and Wales unless it says otherwise.
        </li>
        <li>Not a qualification. Finishing a course does not certify anything.</li>
        <li>Not a mark scheme. Employers score their own tests in their own way.</li>
        <li>
          Not yet reviewed. These scenarios are first versions. They have not been checked by a consent educator, a
          lawyer or a recruiter.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Using this site, or completing any part of it, does not show that a person understands or follows what it
        teaches. It is not evidence of good character, and it is not a defence. Nothing here may be relied on to
        excuse, justify or defend antisocial, abusive, discriminatory or unlawful behaviour, by the person who used
        the site or by anyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everyone remains fully responsible for their own choices and actions. Good Call and Diluted Stories accept no
        responsibility for how this material is used, or for any decision made or action taken because of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The scenarios are fictional. Any resemblance to real people or events is coincidental. If you are in danger,
        or someone else is, call 999.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section prose" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <h2 id="privacy-title">Your privacy</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need an account to use Good Call. Your name, character, answers, points, time spent and reading
        settings are saved on this device only, in your browser's storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not share your data or keep a record of it. Your answers are never used to build a profile of you, so
        they cannot be used to assess you, rank you, target you or discriminate against you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only exception is if you are registered through an institution on our education plan for schools,
        colleges and NGOs. Your institution can tell you what is shared with it and why.
      </p>
      <p>
        You get one go at each scenario. Once you lock in an answer it cannot be changed, so your result is your real
        first judgement. To remove your answers from one course, use "Clear my answers and start again" at the end of
        it. To remove everything, use "Delete all my Good Call data" on your profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every item Good Call saves in your browser is listed on the <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> page, where you can
        also clear them.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
